The variants show how strongly a score depends on the particular facts of a task. Across the tasks within a scenario, the median range of a leading model’s score is 0.34–0.44, and this range exceeds 0.5 in 6–8 of the 20 scenarios.

\subsection{Higher Spending and Effort Do Not Consistently Correspond to Higher Scores}
Cost and effort explain little of the ranking (Figure 5b). GPT-6.1 Sol spends USD 0.24 and 25 turns per run and scores 0.37, whereas Gemini 3.8 Flash spends USD 1.54 and 121 turns and scores 0.19. Qwen 3.8 Flash works longest, at 169 turns and 110 minutes per run, submits within the limits on only 11 of its 152 task–instruction-level combinations, and scores 0.07; GLM-5.3 Flash submits on 95. The three leading models submit on every combination, in 26–60 turns. Recognizing when the work is complete appears to be part of the required skill. %

