Our results establish a worst-case computational barrier to evaluating
the optimal IB tradeoff even when the joint distribution is explicitly
known and arbitrary stochastic encoders are allowed. They delimit the
accuracy guarantees attainable in polynomial time on general inputs and
motivate the study of tractable distribution classes; 
the complexity of approximation within a constant additive error
of \eqref{eq:IB_def} and \eqref{eq:L_beta_def}
remains open.


