\begin{equation}\label{eq:W_def}
    W(y\mid x)=P_{Y\mid X}(y\mid x),\quad\forall x\in\cX\text{ and } y\in \cY.
\end{equation}
The channel $W$ maps every probability distribution $P$ on $\cX$ to the
probability distribution $WP$ on $\cY$ defined by
\begin{equation}
    (WP)(y)=\sum_{x\in \cX} W(y\mid x)P(x),\quad \forall y\in \cY.
\end{equation}
In particular, $WP_X=P_Y$.

